.TH SSOOSSH.YAML 5 "2026-08-16" "ssoossh" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
ssoossh.yaml \- configuration file for the ssoossh client
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ssoossh.yaml
is a YAML file configuring the
.BR ssoossh (1)
client: which server to talk to, how to store keys and certificates, and
which key algorithm to generate.
.SH LOCATION AND MERGING
Unless
.BR "ssoossh --config " \fIfile\fR
is given, up to four files are merged, each layered on top of the last so
later ones override earlier ones on any key both set:
.IP 1. 4
Built-in defaults (compiled into the binary; not a file on disk).
.IP 2. 4
.I /etc/ssoossh/ssoossh.yaml
\(em the system-wide file. This is also the only location the
.B enforce
key (below) is read from.
.IP 3. 4
The per-user file:
.I ~/.config/ssoossh.yaml
on Linux and macOS, or
.I %AppData%\essoossh\essoossh.yaml
(the roaming profile) on Windows. Skipped if no home directory can be
determined.
.IP 4. 4
.I ./ssoossh.yaml
in the current working directory, for development.
.PP
If
.B --config
.I file
is given, that file is merged last, on top of all of the above (except
.BR enforce ,
which still wins over everything \(em see below).
.PP
Command-line flags override every file: currently
.B --server
(overrides
.BR server )
and, for
.B "ssoossh ssh login"
only,
.B --key-type
/
.B --key-size
(override
.B sshkey.type
/
.BR sshkey.size ).
.SS enforce
If the system file
.RI ( /etc/ssoossh/ssoossh.yaml )
sets
.BR enforce ,
naming another YAML file, that file is merged last of all \(em after the
per-user file, the local file, and
.B --config
\(em so it wins over every location a non-administrator can write to. A
relative
.B enforce
path resolves inside the system directory, so it cannot be redirected to a
file the user controls. No file other than the system file may set
.BR enforce ;
setting it anywhere else has no special effect (it is just an ordinary,
unrecognized-by-anything-else key).
.PP
The only setting that currently behaves differently when it arrives via
.B enforce
is
.BR fips :
see below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI server: " url"
Base URL of the ssoosshd server, including scheme, e.g.
.IR https://ssoosshd.example.com .
Overridable per-invocation with
.BR --server .
No default; required for any command that talks to the server.
.TP
.BI capubkey: " string"
The server's CA public key, in
.BR authorized_keys (5)
format. When set, the client skips fetching the CA key from the server at
startup. When empty (the default), it is fetched from the server once per
invocation via
.BR "ssoossh ca" 's
underlying call.
.TP
.BI insecure_skip_verify: " bool"
Skip TLS certificate verification when talking to
.BR server .
Default:
.BR false .
Intended for testing only.
.TP
.B sshkey:
Selects the algorithm and size of the keypair generated for each new
certificate (a fresh keypair is generated every time one is needed, so this
is not a long-lived identity file). Both sub-keys are optional.
.RS
.TP
.BI "  type: " ed25519 | ecdsa | rsa
Key algorithm. Default: \fBed25519\fR normally, or \fBecdsa\fR when FIPS
steering is in effect (see
.B fips
below) \(em ed25519 only entered FIPS 186-5 in 2023 and several FIPS
policies still reject it outright.
.IP
Choosing a non-FIPS-approved type while FIPS steering is in effect produces
a warning, not a refusal, unless FIPS was locked on specifically via
.B enforce
(see
.BR fips ),
in which case it is a hard error at config-load time.
.TP
.BI "  size: " int
Meaning depends on
.BR type :
ignored for \fBed25519\fR (which has exactly one size, and a nonzero value
here only produces a warning); the NIST curve \(em 256, 384, or 521 \(em
for \fBecdsa\fR (default 256); the RSA modulus in bits, minimum 2048, for
.B rsa
(default 3072). RSA key generation costs on the order of hundreds of
milliseconds and is highly variable; ecdsa and ed25519 are effectively
instant. Since a fresh key is generated on every certificate request, this
cost is paid every time, not once.
.RE
.TP
.BI use_agent: " bool"
Keep keys and certificates in a running
.BR ssh-agent (1)
rather than in files. Default:
.BR true ,
and the recommended mode \(em it is also the only mode
.B "ssh proxycommand"
supports, since
.BR ssh (1)
reads key files once at startup and never sees a certificate written after
that. Setting this to false means the agent is not consulted at all, not
merely deprioritized.
.TP
.BI fallback_file_agent: " bool"
When
.B use_agent
is true but no agent is reachable, fall back to file-based storage instead
of failing. Default:
.BR true .
Has no effect when
.B use_agent
is false, since file storage is already in use in that case.
.TP
.BI key_filename: " string"
Base filename (or path) for key/certificate files when file-based storage
is in use, either because
.B use_agent
is false or because it fell back per
.BR fallback_file_agent .
Default:
.BR ssoossh .
.TP
.BI try_open_browser: " bool"
Best-effort automatic launch of the system browser to the approval URL
during
.BR "ssh login" .
The URL is always printed regardless of this setting, so a headless machine
with no browser can still complete a login by hand; a launch failure is
reported and otherwise ignored. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.BI fips: " bool"
Steers key generation toward algorithms SSH implementations running in
FIPS mode generally accept. Advisory only: it changes the default
.B sshkey.type
and warns about non-approved explicit choices, but never refuses one \(em
except when set specifically via the system
.B enforce
mechanism (see
.BR "LOCATION AND MERGING" ),
in which case an unapproved
.B sshkey.type
becomes a hard error instead of a warning.
.IP
Left unset (the default), this follows whether the running binary itself
was built and is running in Go's FIPS 140-3 mode \(em set it explicitly to
target a FIPS-mode server from a client that is not itself running in FIPS
mode.
.TP
.BI enforce: " filename"
Only meaningful in the system file,
.IR /etc/ssoossh/ssoossh.yaml ;
see
.B "LOCATION AND MERGING"
above.
.TP
.BI username: " string"
Present in the schema but currently read by nothing in the client. Reserved
for naming a service account; not yet wired to any behavior.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
insecure_skip_verify: false

use_agent: true
fallback_file_agent: true
key_filename: ssoossh
try_open_browser: false
# enforce: ssoossh-locked.yaml

# fips: true

sshkey:
  type: ed25519
  size: 0
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssoossh (1),
.BR ssh-agent (1),
.BR authorized_keys (5)
